// Adjacent to 0904: the same current-request correlation on the left, but
// with NO rigid filter (`C`) — so the §5.3 `((A S B) ∧ C) ∨ B` rewrite does
// NOT fire (there are no lifted left units) and the backend alone must handle
// the SAME-STEP anchor: at the anchor's own timepoint the left is checked
// over the empty range `(i, i]` and is vacuously true, so the verdict is
// PERMIT regardless of the correlation.
//
// This exposes the temporal engine same-step compensation gap: the verdict read UNIONs
// an inline evaluation of the anchor subplan (the just-inserted anchor row is
// snapshot-invisible), and that compensation projected the correlation
// column as raw NULL — which the outer strict join against the current
// request's binding rejects → wrong DENY at @0. In 0904 the rigid `C` made
// the §5.3 vacuity disjunct supply the row instead, masking this.
//
// @10 pins the history path (guard streak for dave holds over (0,1]) and
// @20 is the deny control (dave's event breaks eve's streak).
//
// Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out). Found by differential
// review of the temporal-compiler since compensation paths.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
